  "result": "Fixed: `--help` now shows short option names before long ones (`-v, --verbose` instead of `--verbose, -v`).\n\nThe change is one line in `src/click/formatting.py:319`. `join_options` sorted the option names with `reverse=True`, which put `--` names first; I removed that flag.\n\n- **Tests:** 1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed. About 31,000 tests were deselected by the project's pytest setup, so those didn't run. No tests had to change.\n- **Manual check:** a command declared with `@click.option('--verbose', '-v', ...)` now shows `-v, --verbose  Be loud.` in its help.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry or commit anything; I can do either if you want.",
